== fuller page ==
Floor 5 is running [five]. It is the host's word for "the lights are on":
the floors below have done their part, and from here, as the host sees it, it
is simply running [hostrunning].

How does a host get there today? When you log in, the start-up file gw.rc
loads the library and asks it to say its name. If it answers, gw.rc brings the
spokes up [spokes]: for each spoke, the library checks whether it is ready,
and if not, mounts it over the network with sshfs [sshfs]. Just before that
part, the file leaves a note in its own voice: "wheels-up!" [wheels].

Here is what is built and what is not. The library and its start-up file
exist, and they are free software. Pin has two notes on which licence: the
library's first lines say "GPLv3+", and the LICENSE file beside it holds the
GNU Affero GPL, version 3 [licence]. Both are kept; the difference is worth
asking about. The floor names are in the library, but no test is attached to
floors 1 to 5 yet [count], so running today is a name and a promise, not a
checked state. C4's language book is blunt about gaps like this: "A tool that
never graduates toward a higher level of assurance is itself a smell" [smell].

As the host sees it, running is the top. Anything that climbs higher does it
on pretend floors, over the page.

